OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Tue 20 Oct to Thu 29 Oct
OL,6,FThere are growing signs that high
OL,7,Fpressure, which is likely to still
OL,8,Fextend across the country at the start
OL,9,Fof this period, will reduce in its
OL,10,Finfluence through next week. This will
OL,11,Fallow a more unsettled regime to
OL,12,Fdevelop as spells of wet and windy
OL,13,Fweather arrive from the Atlantic
OL,14,Ffollowed by drier though still showery
OL,15,Finterludes. While there is still a
OL,16,Fchance that high pressure will build
OL,17,Fnear the UK again during late October,
OL,18,Fit is more likely that a changeable
OL,19,Fregime will continue once established.
OL,20,FThis would see temperature varying
OL,21,Faround average with some milder
OL,22,Fspells, especially in the south.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
PN,16303
SC,0003
CT,20,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F163A1792072101
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G3/3
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Fri 30 Oct to Fri 13 Nov
OL,6,FWeather patterns dominanted by
OL,7,Fwesterly or southwesterly winds from
OL,8,Fthe Atlantic are most likely during
OL,9,FNovember. This resulting in occasional
OL,10,Fspells of wet and windy weather
OL,11,Ffollowed by drier but still showery
OL,12,Finterludes. High pressure may attempt
OL,13,Fto build across the country at times
OL,14,Fbut any settled spells are most likely
OL,15,Fto be short-lived. Temperatures are
OL,16,Flikely to be near or above average
OL,17,Foverall.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
